# i18n collaboratory

Reviewed translations for this app live in the i18n collaboratory. This repo remains the runtime source of truth for how the app loads strings. The hub holds the review copy: English on the left (read-only for reviewers), one locale at a time on the right.

## Changing copy

- Change English in this repo, then send the catalog to the hub. Approval is valid only while the English UTF-8 text still matches the SHA-256 hex stored at approve time (`en_fp`). Unchanged English keeps the stamp. Changed English marks that key stale (`en_source_changed`) until a reviewer approves again. Saving a translation in the hub clears that key’s approval.
- Give every locale the same key tree. A key missing from a locale is exported as an empty string.
- Leave interpolation tokens unchanged (`{{name}}`, `{name}`, ICU). A renamed token is an English change that every locale must follow.
- A leaf is a bare string. `{text, note}` is a leaf only when this project’s hub flag `rich_text` is on. Nested objects are walked. 0-based arrays use decimal segments including `0` (`items.0.text`). 1-based numbered objects (`"1"`, `"2"`, …) must round-trip as objects, not `[null, …]`. Keys starting with `_` are skipped.

## Changing translations

- Reviewers edit in the collaboratory. Bring text back with an admin push-to-repo or a locales zip, then unpack into this repo’s layout when the app does not already use one `{locale}.json` per locale.
- A hub push overwrites `{locale}.json` under the project’s locales path, writes `manifest.json`, and on plain-text projects also writes `{locale}.notes.json`. Ingest skips `*.notes.json` and `manifest.json`.
- Export writes the current text of every key, including drafts. `manifest.json` field `unapproved` counts keys that are missing, unapproved, or stale. A non-zero count means review is unfinished.
- The same `versionHash` twice is a no-op. `initialApproval` (`approved` or `unapproved`, default `unapproved`) applies only on the first ingest, while the project has no head version yet.

## Wiring

Copy `push-catalogs.yml` and `push-catalogs.mjs` from the collaboratory `scripts/templates/`. Site secrets: `I18N_INGEST_URL`, `I18N_PUSH_SECRET`. Actions variable: `I18N_PROJECT_SLUG`. Point `LOCALES_DIR` at the flat interchange directory. If this app stores more than one JSON file per locale, pack before ingest and unpack after export. Leave the shared ingest function unchanged.

Match the hub project to this app: `source_locale` (usually `en`), `placeholder_style` (`i18next`, `icu`, `single-brace`, or `auto`), and `rich_text` only when leaves contain HTML whose tags reviewers must not retype. Markdown or placeholder-only catalogs stay `rich_text` off. With `rich_text` on, reviewers edit words; English tags and link targets are reapplied on save.

The push secret and the hub’s GitHub token stay out of this repo. Procedure for first connect, pack/unpack, and pull-back: the `i18n-collaboratory` skill.
